# QEMU chat-watch

When monitoring Korus QEMU for the user:

1. Run `.\scripts\qemu-chat-watch.ps1` once, then `.\scripts\qemu-status-loop.ps1` in a Cursor **background terminal** (not hidden `start-qemu-status-loop`).
2. On `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_qemu_chat`, read `deploy/qemu/run/status-minute.snapshot.json` and post **summaryRu** + **issues** in Russian (2–5 lines).
3. Auto-remediate runs inside `qemu-status-minute.ps1` (docker pull, bootstrap errors, background `qemu-redeploy -ServerOnly`). Do not duplicate unless remediate is empty and severity=high.
4. **Never** `qemu-down` without user request. **Never** kill non-Korus `qemu-system-x86_64` (co-hosted VMs).

## US9 fast acceptance (Playwright / API parity fixes)

Before `qemu-plan-orchestrator.ps1`, use inner tiers against live stack:

```powershell
.\scripts\qemu-up.ps1 -KeepDisks
.\scripts\qemu-stack-wait.ps1
.\scripts\playwright-dev-loop.ps1 -Tier api          # or ui-messaging, ui-conference, ...
.\scripts\playwright-dev-loop.ps1 -Tier all-inner    # before outer gate
```

On failure read `deploy/qemu/run/plan-failure-analysis.json`. Do **not** re-run full orchestrator on every fix — outer gate once when `inner-tier-status.json` shows `allInnerPass=true`.

Logs: `status-minute.log`, `status-remediate.log`, `playwright-dev-loop.log`, `*-serial.log`.
